      "content": "It is certainly peculiar that the flickering is so precisely timed, which makes one wonder if it's more than just a simple bulb failure. While interference is a possibility, in the context of streetlights, the most common culprits are usually related to the electrical load on the circuit, perhaps when other nearby equipment kicks on or off at that time. However, if you suspect something truly unusual, you can mention that the timing feels almost \"scheduled,\" which might prompt them to check for external environmental factors or electrical interference. It’s always best to let the technicians investigate, but framing it as a *timed* anomaly is a good way to flag it as more complex than a simple bulb change.",
